# Source files are LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact data: never convert line endings or apply any filter.
fixtures/** -text -diff
corpus/** -text -diff
*.bin -text -diff
*.exr binary
*.png binary
*.icc binary
*.icm binary

# Registers: cards that run in parallel add entries at the same places, and `cargo xtask land`
# replays each card's commits one by one onto phase0.
# - docs/improvements.md merges entry by entry with `cargo xtask merge-register`, the
#   `ocio-register` driver: `xtask land` configures it for its replays; for your own
#   cherry-picks and merges, pass
#   `git -c merge.ocio-register.driver="cargo xtask merge-register %O %A %B" cherry-pick ...`.
#   Without it, git merges the file as text and stops on a conflict. (A union merge used to
#   keep both sides' lines here, and attached a removed status block to the wrong entry.)
# - docs/deviations.md is a table that only grows: a union merge keeps both sides' rows. Check
#   the result when a card lands: if two cards edited the same row, both versions are kept.
docs/improvements.md merge=ocio-register
docs/deviations.md merge=union
